            {
              "type": "statichtml",
              "inputClass": "col-md-12",
              "html": "<div ng-hide=\"completed\">\n<p>Requests for PTO will be submitted in 3 phases this year and approved based on company seniority using the same Round Robin approach as last year. This request must be at least 1 full week, individual days will not be accepted. Phase 1 will be a<span>&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: #fa0202;\"><span class=\"text-red\"><u><b>maximum</b></u></span>&nbsp;</span>of 2 weeks, as long as all days are consecutive scheduled work days. Requests less than 1 week will not be considered.</p>\n</div>\n<div ng-hide=\"completed\">\n<h4>Phase 1 Instructions</h4>\nYou may submit as many full week (consecutive event) requests as you would like, however only 1 event will be approved. Requests less than 1 week will not be considered. Please make sure to list your most important week as your 1st event and your least critical week as your<span>&nbsp;</span><span ng-show=\"showmore\" class=\"\">last event. If you select Partial Approval and we cannot approve your full request, we will approve the available dates and place you on the waiting list for unavailable dates. If you select I Do Not Want Partial Approval and we cannot fulfill your request you will not be approved or wait listed for any dates requested and we will try to fulfill your next available request.<br><br>Please review and pay close attention to the dates you are requesting. Do not include days that you are not scheduled to work.<br><br><strong>Weekend Team:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>If you work a weekend there is a limit of 4 Saturdays and/or 4 Sundays you can request off during all 3 Phases of the PTO Process. Please track the total number of Saturdays and Sundays you request off before submitting your form for each Phase.<br><br>This is a combination of 4 Saturdays and/or 4 Sundays for all 3 Phases. After the round robin process is complete, you may request off any remaining Saturdays or Sundays on a first come first served basis. For those of you on 3rd shift who work both Saturday and Sunday, you may request off 4 Saturdays and 4 Sundays during the Round Robin.<br><br>Please do not submit your phase 2 requests at this time. An email will be sent to let you know when you may submit these requests upon completion of Phase 1. You will have an opportunity to view the calendar to see available dates before submitting your Phase 2 requests.<br></span></div>",
              "htmlID": "html2",
              "editorStyle": "editor"
            },
